Setup: global Oolite-style object {cargo:42}. The adapter obtains its
canonical JSValue from the global, calls JS_Dup to retain ownership, drops
the original handle, deletes the global property, reads cargo=42 from the
retained handle, then frees the retained handle. Result RC 0 on AC090 guest.

This is explicit JSTask-owned retention; not transparent compatibility for
SpiderMonkey's pointer-based JS_AddValueRoot/JS_RemoveValueRoot APIs. All
old handles are invalid after OOGFOSJSReset and must be cleared by callers.
